{
 "note": "R107 (P1, review 2026-09-26) - neutral characterisation of `rendering/logo/texlib_{x}_{y}_{z}` on X360 / PS3 Legacy and NHL 15, against\nthe kit families (jersey / pant / sock / nameplate) and the centre-ice family. Read-only over the loose trees (the R104 identity samples\nshowed loose = unwrapped member for every family on these four trees; this probe does not re-derive precedence).\n\nPer member (RW4, first 128 KB; full read only when a descriptor lies beyond): file table, name dictionary (0xEC0010: name -> descriptor\nchunk index) and each 0x20003 raster descriptor decoded with the layouts the developer reader documents (read, not edited):\n  X360 RW4xb2 descriptor: +35 u8 format (0x52 DXT1 / 0x53 DXT3 / 0x54 DXT5, other values recorded raw), +37 u8 h -> (h+1)*8,\n                          +38 u16 w -> (w+1) & 0x1FFF        (crates/tdb-rx2/src/texlib.rs module doc)\n  PS3  RW4ps3 descriptor: +32..43 signature (low u16 of the u32 words at +32 / +36 / +40: 0x6007 0x6007 0x8035 = ARGB8; 0x83F3 0x83F3 0xFFFF = DXT5; others recorded raw),\n                          +48 u16 w, +50 u16 h, +52 u8 mips   (crates/tdb-rx2/src/texlib_ps3.rs module doc)\nReported per family: members, rasters per member, raster name pattern (digits -> #) and for each name suffix (the trailing index k of\n`logo_{a}_{b}_{c}_{k}` or the `_cm/_nm/_sm` role) the (w, h, format) distribution; tuple intersections of the logo family with each kit\nfamily's file tuples (id, style, variant) with full residual counts both ways; logo ids vs centre-ice ids.\nConsumer search (bounded, typed-string only): every loose file under the tree root smaller than 8 MB whose extension is not a texture /\nmesh / audio / archive container, scanned for `rendering/logo`, `logo/texlib`, `texlib_%`, `logo_%`, `%d_%d_%d`; hits listed with path +\ncontext. A miss is a scoped negative (executables are encrypted / not scanned; archive members not scanned).\nUsage: python r107_logo_family_characterisation.py <out.json>\n",
